1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,844
'ok.' With
the period.

2
00:00:02,864 --> 00:00:03,310
You know.

3
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:04,470
They typed 'ok'.

4
00:00:04,490 --> 00:00:06,310
Paused. Added
the period.

5
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:08,200
That pause is
the message.

6
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:09,280
Same question.

7
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,360
Three answers.

8
00:00:11,968 --> 00:00:13,568
'okay': happy.

9
00:00:13,588 --> 00:00:14,748
'ok': busy.

10
00:00:14,768 --> 00:00:16,928
'ok.': you
forgot something.

11
00:00:19,744 --> 00:00:21,144
Except.

12
00:00:21,164 --> 00:00:23,750
This rule breaks for
one kind of person.

13
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:26,330
Some people end
every text with a

14
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,690
period. Your dad.

15
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:28,650
Your boss.

16
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:30,230
Their 'ok.'
is just 'ok'.

17
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:31,392
Pattern first.

18
00:00:31,412 --> 00:00:32,031
Now you.

19
00:00:32,052 --> 00:00:33,772
Which one is
mad at you?

20
00:00:33,792 --> 00:00:35,272
A… or B?

21
00:00:35,956 --> 00:00:39,014
A. First period
she's ever used.

22
00:00:39,034 --> 00:00:41,014
Bonus: a lone
'k' isn't anger.

23
00:00:41,034 --> 00:00:42,214
It's a door closing.

24
00:00:42,234 --> 00:00:44,194
2/7: left on read.

